    "use_ik_match_table1": true,
    "use_ik_match_table2": true,
    "_comment_rot_offsets": "Derived from bvh_lafan1_to_n1.json by applying per-joint bridge quaternions q_bridge[j] = q_H_SOMA[j]^-1 * q_H_LAFAN1[j], extracted from the validated bvh_soma_to_g1.json and cleaned / symmetrised. LeftArm / RightArm are now tracked on *upper_arm_yaw_link* (3 DoFs upstream: shoulder_pitch + roll + yaw) instead of *upper_arm_roll_link* (2 DoFs), because A-pose-calibrated SOMA motions carry substantial humeral rotation that can only be matched with all three shoulder DoFs. Rest orientation is identical between the two links (yaw_joint = 0 at rest), so the existing rot_offset still applies. Shoulder rot_w reduced to 10 (LAFAN1/SMPLX convention). Ankle and torso adjustments carry over from bvh_soma_to_g1.json. Trunk rot_w lowered to 10 (matches the corresponding LAFAN1 config) so the torso isn't artificially held upright during motion.",
    "_comment_scales": "Per-segment scales: Hips/Chest/Legs/Feet tuned so SOMA A-pose pelvis and ankles land on N1's rest geometry (pelvis 0.700 m, ankle 0.045 m vs SOMA pelvis 1.010 m, ankle 0.07 m). Arms raised from the strict radial ratio (~0.71) to 0.8, matching bvh_lafan1_to_n1.json: N1 has relatively wide shoulders (0.351 m shoulder-to-shoulder vs SOMA 0.327 m) so scaling SOMA's arm positions down too far produces targets tighter than the robot's physical width, leaving arms parked near rest and giving the silhouette a slightly-wider-than-reference feel. 0.8 (same as LAFAN1) keeps arm targets in a range IK can actually track. Hips = 0.688 (0.005 lower than Chest = 0.693): without this, initial-frame feet sat ~+8 mm above the floor; lowering just the Hips scale drops the pelvis (and the stance with it) by ~0.5 cm in world z so feet land within +-3 mm of the floor during the first frames, without needing to touch ground_height. Walking-stride compression from this asymmetry is <1 %. Validated: walking / jumping / dancing keep feet at z>=0 with no NaNs.",
    "human_scale_table": {
        "Hips": 0.688,
        "Chest": 0.693,
        "LeftLeg": 0.697,
        "RightLeg": 0.697,
